uptions you  know divide up our ability to pay  attention and and do our work so what  are tips you might have to to keep  people productive  despite this may lay all around them  yeah I mean first of all we we surveyed  professionals that asked him what kind  of interruptions whether they were  having interruptions and what they were  like nearly a third said that they were  have being interrupted by family members  the next step was technology challenges  that we're interrupting them and then it  was pets spouses and  and kids so there are all kinds of  problems that we face at home what we  have heard from members about how they  deal with it are number one they are  trying to make sure that they have a  regimented approach to their day and  that they are talking to their family  about it here's what my day is like here  the hours that I can work I can tell you  that my wife and I have a intricate  schedule for when she is running her  company and when I'm trying to do my job  and when we were homeschooling our three  kids so we try to make it work we go  over the schedules in the morning we  hear a lot of people saying they're  doing that and they are also trying to  make sure that they have a very segment  and on what part of their day is work  and what part of their day is family so  that you can close the computer at some  point and say I'm dumb even though I'm  walking two feet away from where I was  just working I am now in family mode  rather than in work mode yeah yeah  important distinction  all right so putting aside productivity  let's talk about creativity we mentioned  the break room earlier the break room is  actually a place where you might share  an idea get some feedback I mean it can  be a productive moment without that  interaction with a colleague how can you  inspire creativity when you're at home  yeah I mean there are a lot of people  who are being trying to be as creative  as the cam was still having those  unscripted moments with colleagu